+// Blocked hosts (content_blocking_hosts, ABI 1.69): what ReArcTabGetBlockedCount
+// counts, by site, for a "Blocked on this page" list. *json is +1 malloc,
+// NUL-terminated UTF-8; free with ReArcBufferFree.
+//   {"page":{"host":"example.com","registrable":true},
+//    "hosts":[{"host":"doubleclick.net","count":3,"registrable":true,
+//              "lists":["easylist"]}],"more":0}
+// page: the tab's own site, named as a blocked one is, from the primary main
+// frame's committed address; absent when that is not http or https. A host
+// that writes a rule "allow this host on this site" takes both names from one
+// reply, and reads the reply again before it writes: if page has changed, the
+// tab has moved on and nothing is written.
+// host: the registrable domain of a blocked request's host (private
+// registries count: "someone.github.io"), lower-case ASCII (punycode); the
+// host itself when it has no registrable domain. registrable: the name is
+// one site, a registrable domain or an IP address; false for a single-label
+// name and for a public suffix ("co.uk"), which a host must never turn into
+// a rule. count: requests blocked for it. lists: the bundle's ids of the
+// lists whose rules blocked them, "_dynamic" for the person's own rules.
+// more: blocked requests whose site is not listed (at most 100 sites; a host
+// that cannot be kept). Hosts are in no order the host may rely on.
+// The page chooses the hosts it asks for: a host treats every name as
+// untrusted text. The engine keeps the sites in memory only, beside the
+// count, and drops them with it: at a main frame navigation to another
+// document, with the tab, with the blocker. Nothing else of a request is
+// kept. An unknown tab: {"hosts":[],"more":0}. Blocking off or nothing
+// blocked: no hosts, and page as above. Null json: invalid_argument. No new callback:
+// ReArcBlockedCountCallback says when the answer changed.
+REARC_ENGINE_EXPORT ReArcStatus ReArcTabCopyBlockedHosts(uint64_t tab_id,
+                                                         char** json);
+
+// Host sites (host_sites, ABI 1.69): the site of a host, by Chromium's public
+// suffix list, for a host that keeps something per site (a blocking
+// exception, a boost's scope, the part of a long host an address line must
+// keep) and has no suffix list of its own. *json is +1 malloc, NUL-terminated
+// UTF-8; free with ReArcBufferFree.
+//   {"host":"example.co.uk","registrable":true,"suffix":false}
+// host and registrable are what ReArcTabCopyBlockedHosts gives for a blocked
+// request to utf8_host: host is the registrable domain, private registries
+// included, or the name itself when it has none; registrable is false for a
+// single-label name and for a public suffix. suffix: the name is itself a
+// public suffix ("com", "co.uk", "web.app", "edu.au"): every site under it is
+// another party's, so it must never become the key of a rule, an exception
+// or a scope. registrable false and suffix false: a name with no suffix at
+// all ("localhost", an intranet's "wiki"). An IPv4 address is itself, with
+// registrable true. utf8_host: a DNS name or IPv4 address of at most 253 bytes, ASCII
+// letters, digits, '.', '-' and '_' (an international name in its xn-- form);
+// a trailing dot is dropped. Anything else, a scheme, a port, a path or an
+// IPv6 literal among it: invalid_argument, and *json null. So is a name the
+// engine reads as another one ("1.2", "0x7f.1": addresses in short forms):
+// host is always the asked name, lower case, or the end of it. Synchronous, a
+// table lookup: it asks nothing of the network or of any profile.
+REARC_ENGINE_EXPORT ReArcStatus ReArcEngineCopySiteOfHost(const char* utf8_host,
+                                                          char** json);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }  // extern "C"
 #endif
